WEBVTT

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:06.930
No way I'm gonna let this end so easily...

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.470
Y-Yeah!

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:19.320
Class A wins.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.800
What's going on? Rep?

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.440
Huh?

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:41.850
Something that grows when its alone, What is it?

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.130
One more chance, One more chance!

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:44.510
Never, Never give up!

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:45.810
One more chance, One more chance!

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:47.110
Never give up!

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:00.240
Meeting with someone else is easy

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:03.010
I decided what to say before they even asked

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:05.620
My heart beats fast thinking if I passed or not

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:07.800
I can't panic in this fight for love

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:10.870
Study! Study! Study! Keeps me up all night

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.500
I've got a dreaming genius inside me

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.080
I'd be great if everyone's wishes came true

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.250
I won't care about other people's lives

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.210
Perfect-area complete!

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:23.840
I'll definitely be waiting for you!

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:30.240
I can hear your voice from the Perfect-area!

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.550
Ah! Ear! Ear!

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:34.820
Why? Why can't stop when I pass you

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.430
if I'm your counselor

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:40.020
"Are we friends?" Yes, we're friends."

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:42.020
But, I failed the test with a 0

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:45.330
No! I'll take it again! and again!

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.470
I'm serious. One more chance, please

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:51.940
There's something better for is in the future

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:58.030
Better than my life right now.

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:06.490
The ESB is over and a new morning has arrived.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.810
Could these be...

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:12.970
Yeah, they're drawing boards and mats.

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:14.760
Thirteenth Period
Idiots and Tests and Summoned Beings

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:18.830
And I thought cardboard boxes were the bottom of the barrel.

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:20.820
There's no end to the worse.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:22.070
I never imagined this happening.

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:23.440
Sorry, Himeji.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:27.680
Don't be. You really don't need to apologize.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.360
I had a lot of fun from the ESB.

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:32.030
Himeji...

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.360
Cheer up, all of you!

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:36.370
It's not like we can do anything about losing.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:39.120
These drawing boards are definitely usable.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.070
Well, they say you can get used to living anywhere.

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:45.100
It's like we're in art class. It's not that bad.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:47.120
What's the matter, Mizuki?

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:48.670
Well, umm...

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:50.590
I can't see the bottom of the board.

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:53.390
Where are you going, Minami?

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:57.100
Do you really need to ask? Of course I'm going to request another ESB!

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.050
Just give up, Shimada!

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:01.790
We're banned from doing so for another three months!

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:04.700
But... I just don't want to use these boards anymore!

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:07.190
Well, your breasts won't get in your way, so these are a perfect fit for-

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:09.050
My joints don't work that way!

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:10.740
Somehow I haven't felt this in a long time.

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:13.700
What do you mean "these are a perfect fit!?"

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:21.840
Almost... Almost... Just a little...

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:26.590
You're burning! You're on fire, Voyeur!

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:31.390
Wow, it got put out by his blood!

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:35.210
Oh, wow. Is that all it takes to bring you down, Voyeur?

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:36.170
Kudou...

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:40.800
I even wore a bra just for you today.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:42.140
A really cute one.

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:44.040
So what?

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:46.630
The body never lies.

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:49.110
Don't worry! I feel for you, Voyeur!

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:50.560
Awaken!

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:57.070
Oh, sorry... I forgot that the bracelet broke.

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:58.080
Note • Voyeur

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:00.330
Where are you going, Voyeur!?

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:02.790
Please grant summoning permission to Akihisa.

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:04.290
For what reason?

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:06.190
To remove a bra.

00:04:06.190 --> 00:04:07.540
I'm afraid I cannot, then.

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:12.470
So I guess that's as far as our strength goes.

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:14.390
Well, I guess so.

00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:17.430
But I can't accept losing like that.

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:19.590
Well, a defeat is a defeat.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:24.970
We focused more on pragmatism than scoring high on tests.

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:26.650
The same goes for them.

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:31.360
They were smart for attacking instead of being distracted by the situation.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:33.910
We lost because we let our guard down.

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:34.960
But...

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.590
You can't change what has already happened.

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:38.480
Results are everything, after all.

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:46.670
What's the matter, Aki?

00:04:46.670 --> 00:04:51.330
You said that effort is nothing but a means to an end, remember?

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:53.250
Yes, I do.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:55.380
I couldn't do what I needed to do.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.750
Perhaps I'm just an idiot after all...

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:02.550
Those who boast of their own efforts are the most foolish.

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:06.550
But having someone else praise you for your efforts isn't necessarily a bad thing.

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:07.260
Sis...

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:09.760
I believe you tried your very best.

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:13.430
You make me proud to be your sister.

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:14.970
Thank you, Sis...

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:17.770
It's all right to grieve over your defeat.

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:21.280
Don't people normally say to do the opposite?

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:24.820
It's important to admit when you've lost.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:30.050
Not being able to do so makes it impossible for you to climb back up after a fall,

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:32.720
and even more impossible for you to move forward.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:35.890
So go on ahead and grieve to your heart's extent.

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:41.040
But after you're done grieving, be sure to set your eyes upon your next goal and move toward it.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:43.350
Okay.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:48.760
I will comfort you as much as I can when you're grieving.

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:52.520
Would you rather sleep with me or take a bath with me?

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:53.860
No thanks...

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:57.060
Don't be like that.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:58.500
We're related by blood.

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:00.790
That's exactly why I don't want to!

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:07.300
Once you're done grieving, move forward, huh?

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:08.930
Forward?

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:13.230
Does that possibly mean I could still do more?

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:15.550
All right, I've made my decision!

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:18.060
So we'll be taking a bath together, right?

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:19.840
No, I meant something else.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:25.480
That's all for the ESB results.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:27.600
Who is it?

00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:31.180
Yoshii, what the hell are you doing here?

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:32.900
I have a request to make.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:36.430
Please allow us to compete with class A one more time.

00:06:36.430 --> 00:06:38.620
I'm afraid I'll have to turn that request down.

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:41.890
Just wait another three months.

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:43.020
We can't wait that long!

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:46.840
That's the rule. I can't break it.

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:48.310
Please!

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:54.420
I can't let it end like this! Please!

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:56.090
Consider it a request from the rest of us as well.

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:59.810
I cannot accept such a cowardly victory.

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:02.490
Even though we technically won,

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:04.860
I hate to admit it, but they had the upper hand during the fight.

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:07.780
Kinoshita... Kirishima...

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:09.290
You girls...

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:13.000
That victory is an insult to the top class that represents this school.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:17.230
I don't think the rest of the classes will accept this so easily either, so...

00:07:17.230 --> 00:07:18.900
I'll send in my request too.

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:25.320
Do you kids know why the Exam Summoning Battle system was implemented into our school?

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:31.110
I can't give way regarding the rules, but...

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:36.710
I still owe you a favor from when the system went berserk.

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:41.420
And I'm responsible for the fact that you were using the prototype bracelet.

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:45.020
I guess I can make an exception just this once if you're this serious about it.

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:45.840
Exception?

00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:51.090
Do you really want to exchange facilities that bad?

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:55.570
If so, there are other means of achieving that.

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:57.900
What!?

00:07:57.900 --> 00:07:59.660
A rematch with class A?

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:01.370
We really can?

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:04.050
That old bitch allowed it?

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:05.530
That's great, Akihisa!

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:07.210
Yeah...

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:10.390
Hell yeah! We'll beat them into the ground this time!

00:08:10.390 --> 00:08:12.260
Let's hurry and form up a new plan.

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:16.010
Well, Yuuji... It's a bit different this time.

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:19.100
WHAT!?

00:08:19.670 --> 00:08:21.170
You're going solo?

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:25.470
Yeah, against class A's rep in an exam battle.

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:28.650
Class A's rep? You mean Shouko?

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:32.530
We can't exchange facilities if I win,

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:35.320
but the principal promised to grant my request.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:37.330
But you're going against the valedictorian!

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:38.500
Can you win?

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:41.160
Are you sure?

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:43.900
Don't worry, I won't pull you guys down with me.

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:48.080
Akihisa, so what'll happen if you lose?

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:50.820
The other side gets their wish granted-

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:53.810
If I win, you'll have to return my marriage contract.

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:55.490
It isn't yours!

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:57.070
You bastard!

00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:59.460
"I won't pull you guys down with me." Yeah, right!

00:08:59.460 --> 00:08:59.750
This is my life you're fucking with!

00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:01.500
Life

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:03.540
That isn't important!

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:06.220
We're going on a honeymoon right after the match.

00:09:06.470 --> 00:09:07.440
Hell no!

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:09.430
Yuuji, I want to make children with you.

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:13.390
Akihisa, you have to fucking win this, no matter what!

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:16.060
Shouko, take it easy on him, please!

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:20.110
I thought you said not to hold back?

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:24.350
Holy shit! My life is over!

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:26.730
So you're saying that I'm gonna lose for sure.

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:29.780
But I guess he's right...

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:34.680
They granted us a rematch, but there's no way I can beat Kirishima by myself...

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:36.410
Mr. Stupid!

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:38.610
Oh, Hazuki.

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:41.080
Here, this is a present for you.

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:44.470
Wow, you baked cookies!

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:46.640
I learned it from home economics class.

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:48.830
Though I don't think they're that good...

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:50.210
Thank you very much, Hazuki.

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:53.890
Yay! So do you feel a little more confident now?

00:09:55.480 --> 00:09:57.630
I see. Thanks.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:58.760
I feel a lot more energetic now.

00:10:00.270 --> 00:10:02.400
These are good.

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:03.980
You'd make a great wife.

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:05.210
Thank you!

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:08.770
I didn't really quite get the hang of it, so I burned a few batches.

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:11.240
But I didn't give up and kept trying and I succeeded!

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:14.630
All right!

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:17.160
What's the matter?

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:19.710
I'll make sure I don't give up either.

00:10:19.710 --> 00:10:22.320
It's not like I have anything to lose, so I'll give it everything I've got.

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:24.180
Thank you, Hazuki.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:25.680
You're welcome!

00:10:26.820 --> 00:10:27.620
I'm home.

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:29.750
Welcome back, Aki.

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:35.310
I don't know what I can do with the time I have...

00:10:35.310 --> 00:10:39.320
But I'll try my best to get even a single point more.

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:58.980
This is a specially permitted rematch between class A's rep, Shouko Kirishima, and class F's Akihisa Yoshii.

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:01.820
We'll go by the "Sudden Death Rule."

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:01.910
Sudden Death Rule.

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:03.530
Sudden Death Rule
Sudden Death Rule.

00:11:03.530 --> 00:11:03.590
The exact same question will be given to the contestants,
Sudden Death Rule

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:06.550
The exact same question will be given to the contestants,

00:11:06.550 --> 00:11:08.160
and they are required to solve it at the same time.

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:11.540
The battle ends whenever one of the
contestants answers a question wrong.

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:13.620
The loser will be the one who answered it wrong.

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:17.410
In other words, whoever's the first to get a question wrong loses.

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:20.580
We're dealing with an endless series of questions here,

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:22.430
but they'll keep getting harder and harder as they go along.

00:11:22.430 --> 00:11:24.720
That means the beginning will be decisive.

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:26.180
Akihisa...

00:11:26.690 --> 00:11:28.380
All right, let's begin!

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:30.210
Good luck, Akihisa.

00:11:30.530 --> 00:11:31.290
Yuuji...

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:33.310
I believe that you can win.

00:11:33.310 --> 00:11:35.980
You have to believe in yourself and do your best!

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:37.520
FIGHT ON!

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:41.310
He only cheers people on if it benefits himself.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:42.850
Question 1:

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:45.520
Please answer the question with an idiom that contains the given meaning.

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:48.300
"Failing at something you're good at."

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:50.470
That's an easy question.

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:54.840
Unless Akihisa is literally mentally
retarded, he can't screw this one up.

00:11:58.190 --> 00:11:59.600
He looks like he's having trouble!

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:00.470
What!?

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:02.690
What about this?

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:04.540
Quandoque bonus dormitat Homerus
Even monkeys fall from trees

00:12:04.540 --> 00:12:05.710
Yippee!

00:12:05.710 --> 00:12:07.340
Both answers are correct.

00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:09.020
Quandoque bonus dormitat Homerus
Even monkeys fall from trees

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:10.900
Don't fucking scare me, bro!

00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:13.720
I was nervous! I couldn't help it!

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:15.040
Question 2:

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:17.740
How do you calculate the area of a circle?

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:20.680
Radius × Radius × Pi

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:23.350
Yeah! She got it wrong!

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:24.930
Radius × Radius × Pi

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:26.360
Wait, why!?

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:29.110
How did you even get into high school?

00:12:29.110 --> 00:12:29.570
Radius × Radius × Pi

00:12:29.570 --> 00:12:31.360
Next up, question 3.

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:40.240
It's edible, but still a long way from what it should be...

00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:43.330
I bet Aki is trying his best now.

00:12:43.850 --> 00:12:46.700
It'd be great if I could cook
him something as a reward.

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:50.260
I've got to try my best as well.

00:12:50.420 --> 00:12:52.040
Q-Question 30...

00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:56.010
When was the 12 level ranking
system of officials implemented?

00:12:58.150 --> 00:12:59.770
Both answers are correct.

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:03.310
Good going, bro!

00:13:03.310 --> 00:13:04.280
You can do it!

00:13:05.730 --> 00:13:09.030
I managed to make it this far because I had a feeling these questions would show up...

00:13:09.530 --> 00:13:12.030
She's not gonna screw up that easily...

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:14.530
I can't let my guard down for even one question.

00:13:14.740 --> 00:13:16.450
Question 31:

00:13:16.450 --> 00:13:19.920
Who was the conquerer that began his
conquest of the Persian Empire in 334BC

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:25.160
and defeated the last king of the Achaemenid Empire?

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:26.750
Another history question...

00:13:26.750 --> 00:13:28.480
This is a tough one.

00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:29.790
Akihisa...

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:32.030
Alexander the Third
Alexander the Great

00:13:32.030 --> 00:13:33.430
Both answers are correct.

00:13:33.430 --> 00:13:33.600
Alexander the Third
Alexander the Great

00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:35.380
Oh, he got it right!

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:36.800
Good job, Aki!

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:38.170
Alexander the Third
Alexander the Great

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:41.180
I'll never get this question about
Alexander the Great wrong ever again.

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:41.380
Alexander the Third
Alexander the Great

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:44.200
The easy questions are coming to an end.

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:46.770
Answering is only going to get harder and harder for Akihisa.

00:13:46.770 --> 00:13:47.810
Akihisa...

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:49.830
Question 32:

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:52.580
The name of Japan's first era was "Taika."

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:57.070
Which year of the Common Era did the reform of the Taika era take place?

00:13:58.350 --> 00:13:59.460
That question is...

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:01.250
That's a gimme.

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:03.710
Both of them will get this one correct.

00:14:03.930 --> 00:14:05.710
The showdown is delayed until the next question.

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:09.340
What's the matter, Akihisa?

00:14:09.340 --> 00:14:13.230
S-So when exactly did the Taika reforms happen?

00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:15.140
What!?

00:14:15.140 --> 00:14:17.980
You dumbass! How could you forget after we've been through all that crap!?

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:21.360
That's exactly why I'm confused!

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:23.810
Don't fuck with me, you fucking faggot!

00:14:23.810 --> 00:14:27.100
I only remember it according to the "uneventful reforms"...

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:32.650
"Uneventful reforms"... 645AD? 625AD?

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:34.570
Which does "uneventful" refer to?

00:14:35.070 --> 00:14:38.540
Uneventful reforms... Uneventful... Uneventful...

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:40.570
Akihisa...

00:14:40.780 --> 00:14:41.570
Aki.

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:45.110
Which one? Which one is it!?

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:48.520
It's all over if I get this wrong.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:51.830
Aki...

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:54.430
Akihisa...

00:14:55.690 --> 00:14:57.500
God dammit!

00:15:00.770 --> 00:15:01.500
Aki?

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:02.340
Akihisa?

00:15:02.340 --> 00:15:05.110
I'll fucking murder him for giving up so easily...!

00:15:05.390 --> 00:15:07.280
He, he hasn't yet!

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:08.450
That's...

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:17.110
That's Striker Sigma V!

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:19.210
Go!

00:15:19.210 --> 00:15:23.460
Stop it, you dumbass!

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:28.890
Their answers are different!

00:15:28.890 --> 00:15:29.950
What!?

00:15:30.860 --> 00:15:33.810
Shit, my life's over...

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:36.970
The winner is class F's Akihisa Yoshii.

00:15:36.970 --> 00:15:38.320
What the hell!?

00:15:42.660 --> 00:15:44.140
I guessed it right...

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:45.410
Good job, Aki!

00:15:45.410 --> 00:15:46.760
Nice one, Akihisa!

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:48.060
Akihisa!

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:57.060
Shouko, what happened?

00:15:58.340 --> 00:16:01.070
I made a promise with you...

00:16:04.420 --> 00:16:06.740
...that I'd never forget.

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:16.480
I'm sorry.

00:16:17.570 --> 00:16:20.250
Moreover, I already got what I wanted.

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:21.260
What?

00:16:22.510 --> 00:16:24.170
I'm going to go register now.

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:25.680
How the hell did you...!?

00:16:26.070 --> 00:16:27.430
A kind soul gave it to me.

00:16:27.430 --> 00:16:28.500
Don't tell me...

00:16:29.740 --> 00:16:32.020
No harm in doing a good deed here and there.

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:37.120
I can't believe you won.

00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:38.420
Principal...

00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:42.600
As promised, I'll grant you your wish.

00:16:43.050 --> 00:16:44.580
Thank you very much.

00:16:44.580 --> 00:16:48.290
Wish... What did you ask from the principal, Akihisa?

00:16:48.590 --> 00:16:49.130
Well...

00:16:49.130 --> 00:16:50.460
All right then, Himeji.

00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:53.130
You're free to take the placement exam again.

00:16:54.180 --> 00:16:55.890
Akihisa, don't tell me you...

00:16:56.280 --> 00:17:00.700
This is the reason I declared the ESB to begin with.

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:02.400
Even if we don't deserve it ourselves,

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:06.430
we want you to study some-
where that's fitting for you.

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:07.650
Then...

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:10.160
You can now go to the class that matches your ability.

00:17:11.240 --> 00:17:12.830
Isn't that great, Himeji?

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:16.380
No... Akihisa...

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:17.130
Why?

00:17:17.130 --> 00:17:20.570
Akihisa, is this what you really want?

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:25.570
It's gonna feel a little lonely, but this is the best choice to make.

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:28.190
Really?

00:17:29.640 --> 00:17:31.830
Thank you, Akihisa.

00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:37.080
All right, begin.

00:17:44.030 --> 00:17:48.780
A lot of people in this world thinks that grades equate to everything.

00:17:48.780 --> 00:17:54.310
But no matter what, a person's ability can only go so far.

00:17:54.780 --> 00:18:00.320
Those who only care about themselves won't be able to live a fulfilling life.

00:18:00.840 --> 00:18:06.190
When I was a kid, we all helped each other out as a matter of course.

00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:12.620
Something achieved through only one
person's effort isn't really worth that much.

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:16.120
If they understand that, then I can rest easy.

00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:26.840
Time's up.

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:30.190
Looks good.

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:32.550
Now you'll be able to go to class A.

00:18:32.810 --> 00:18:33.470
Thank you.

00:18:33.830 --> 00:18:35.700
I'll give you your results later.

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:37.020
You can go home now.

00:18:38.210 --> 00:18:38.810
Excuse me!

00:18:39.710 --> 00:18:40.320
What's the matter?

00:18:40.820 --> 00:18:43.860
I messed something up big time.

00:18:43.860 --> 00:18:45.240
Could you allow me to change that?

00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:46.800
The time allotted is already over.

00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:48.370
You can't change your answers.

00:18:48.370 --> 00:18:49.060
But...

00:18:49.060 --> 00:18:52.420
Don't worry, I'm sure you did fine.

00:18:52.670 --> 00:18:53.540
Please!

00:18:54.760 --> 00:18:58.700
I have to... I have to amend that no matter what!

00:19:01.360 --> 00:19:02.930
Please!

00:19:07.030 --> 00:19:08.350
Good morning, Aki.

00:19:08.350 --> 00:19:10.540
Morning, Akihisa.

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:11.220
Morning.

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:12.490
Good morning.

00:19:12.850 --> 00:19:13.850
Yoshii...

00:19:13.850 --> 00:19:15.700
Hey, Kirishima.

00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:18.940
We went to get registered, but we got rejected.

00:19:19.070 --> 00:19:19.460
County Clerk
Shouko Image

00:19:19.460 --> 00:19:23.660
According to the Japanese Civil Code, the male must be at least 18 when he registers for marriage.

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:23.960
County Clerk
Shouko Image

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:26.490
That's unfortunate...

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:36.100
Akihisa.

00:19:40.100 --> 00:19:42.490
Aki, have you seen Mizuki yet?

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:44.930
Nope, not yet.

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:46.070
Really...

00:19:46.070 --> 00:19:49.620
It's going to be hard for you two to see each other now that she's in a different class.

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:50.380
I guess.

00:19:50.380 --> 00:19:51.840
Have you heard, Akihisa?

00:19:52.180 --> 00:19:52.930
About what?

00:19:52.930 --> 00:19:57.390
Himeji's score on the placement exam will definitely get her into class A.

00:19:57.390 --> 00:19:58.140
Really?

00:19:58.340 --> 00:19:59.730
Are you sure that's fine?

00:19:59.910 --> 00:20:00.480
Yeah.

00:20:01.100 --> 00:20:03.610
Himeji doesn't belong in class F.

00:20:04.130 --> 00:20:08.240
She should be studying with the
amazing facilities class A has to offer.

00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:11.180
If that's what you think, then okay.

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:15.420
But Akihisa, I don't think things are going to go your way.

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:19.290
Good morning, Akihisa.

00:20:19.510 --> 00:20:22.100
Himeji... Why are you here? Did you forget something?

00:20:22.100 --> 00:20:24.830
No, this is where I belong.

00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:28.110
But aren't you accepted into class A?

00:20:28.110 --> 00:20:32.620
Well, actually... I forgot to write my name.

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:33.390
So I got a zero on the test.

00:20:34.240 --> 00:20:37.900
That's why I'm here back in class F.

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:39.430
Himeji...

00:20:41.230 --> 00:20:46.440
Let's have fun like we used to, okay?

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:50.210
What's the matter, Aki?

00:20:50.210 --> 00:20:51.280
Joys of tear?

00:20:51.280 --> 00:20:53.220
That's great, Akihisa.

00:20:53.220 --> 00:20:54.670
Happy end.

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:58.040
That goddamned old bitch!

00:21:02.520 --> 00:21:11.590
Baka, go go home!

00:21:11.880 --> 00:21:14.860
It's a time of peace now that school's out

00:21:14.860 --> 00:21:16.410
If I were to compare her

00:21:16.410 --> 00:21:17.950
"She's a real angel!"

00:21:17.950 --> 00:21:20.920
Then a sudden note ruined my fun

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:22.310
It said I have a makeup test!

00:21:22.310 --> 00:21:23.700
It's hell!

00:21:24.030 --> 00:21:27.040
I was joking with my friends,

00:21:27.040 --> 00:21:30.070
"There's no way someone is that stupid!"

00:21:30.070 --> 00:21:33.150
But deep down inside,

00:21:33.150 --> 00:21:34.440
I was screaming,

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:37.400
"That was me! I'm that stupid!"

00:21:37.820 --> 00:21:43.980
I thought the "Monthly" sign in the parking lot

00:21:43.980 --> 00:21:49.260
was the company's name!

00:21:49.260 --> 00:21:52.010
For the longest time...

00:21:52.710 --> 00:21:55.710
Stupidity is a manly character

00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:58.410
Is that our lack of common sense?

00:21:58.410 --> 00:22:01.720
Rules are useless in this world

00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:04.720
Eat Korean BBQ every night and overthrow the masses!

00:22:04.720 --> 00:22:06.360
Look!

00:22:06.360 --> 00:22:10.930
The sun that rose from the west is now setting down.

00:22:10.930 --> 00:22:13.970
Run! It's almost dinner time.

00:22:13.970 --> 00:22:20.840
Let's go home!

00:22:28.160 --> 00:22:29.530
You bitch!

00:22:29.930 --> 00:22:32.840
Watch your mouth, you little brat.

00:22:33.120 --> 00:22:34.470
That's not fair!

00:22:34.470 --> 00:22:36.390
Why did Himeji get a zero?

00:22:36.390 --> 00:22:39.570
Well, obviously because she
forgot to write her name down.

00:22:39.870 --> 00:22:41.450
You're kidding me!

00:22:41.450 --> 00:22:46.520
She was the only one taking the test, so it should be obvious that it's her!

00:22:46.520 --> 00:22:48.980
Are you guys blind!?

00:22:48.980 --> 00:22:51.120
You idiot!

00:22:52.710 --> 00:22:56.030
Wow, I never thought I'd live long
enough to hear you call me an idiot.

00:22:56.030 --> 00:22:58.980
Anyway, give Himeji's points back!

00:22:58.980 --> 00:23:01.920
If you can't, then let her take the placement exam again!

00:23:03.590 --> 00:23:06.210
I'm starting to think you're a real idiot.

00:23:07.080 --> 00:23:07.620
Huh?

00:23:10.040 --> 00:23:10.840
What a dumbass.

00:23:10.840 --> 00:23:11.590
You're stupid.

00:23:11.590 --> 00:23:12.670
Idiot.

00:23:12.670 --> 00:23:13.500
Stupid.

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:14.760
You're truly one giant idiot.

00:23:14.760 --> 00:23:15.590
Idiot.

00:23:16.750 --> 00:23:19.880
Akihisa, you're really stupid, aren't you?

00:23:21.270 --> 00:23:23.350
You're the last one I'd expect that from... Why?

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:31.470
Stupid!
